    {
      "name": "3 - Market data",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /market/assets",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/market/assets?q=AAPL&limit=10",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "market",
                "assets"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "AAPL",
                  "description": "Symbol prefix or part of a company name",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "10",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": false
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Symbol lookup for the ticker search box.\n\nAlpaca's assets endpoint has no search parameter, so the match happens\nhere over a cached copy of the active US equity list (see\n`alpaca.active_equity_assets`). An empty query returns an empty list\nrather than the first ten of fourteen thousand arbitrary tickers."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /market/bars/{symbol}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/market/bars/{{symbol}}?timeframe=1Day&limit=200",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "market",
                "bars",
                "{{symbol}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "timeframe",
                  "value": "1Day",
                  "description": "One of 1Day, 1Hour, 15Min, 5Min, 1Min",
                  "disabled": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "200",
                  "description": "",
                  "disabled": false
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "OHLCV candles, oldest first - the order every charting library wants."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /market/clock",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/market/clock",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "market",
                "clock"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Is the market open, and when does that next change?\n\nThe frontend needs this to say \"your order will queue until 9:30 AM\"\ninstead of leaving the user wondering why nothing filled.\n\nUnder the dev weekend override (ADR-019) `is_open` is forced false and\n`simulated` says so: the whole app then behaves as it will on a real\nSaturday. Only this route's answer is faked - everything that records\ndata (the sampler) reads Alpaca's clock directly and never sees this."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /market/quotes/{symbol}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/market/quotes/{{symbol}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "market",
                "quotes",
                "{{symbol}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Latest bid/ask plus the last trade, in one call.\n\nAlpaca splits these across two endpoints because they are two different\nfacts: the quote is what someone will trade at *now*, the trade is what\nsomeone actually paid. A buy preview needs both.\n\nOutside market hours the ask side is often 0 - there is nobody offering."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /market/token/{symbol}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/market/token/{{symbol}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "market",
                "token",
                "{{symbol}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The tokenized twin of a listed share, priced right now on Jupiter.\n\nAn xStock (NVDAx for NVDA) is one real share held in custody, mirrored as\na Solana token that trades around the clock. While the market is open the\ntwo prices track closely; on a weekend the token is the only live price\nthere is, and the distance between them at Monday's first execution is\nwhat the paper's reserve is sized against. This route shows that distance\nlive, as `gap_pct`, beside both prices.\n\n404 `no_token` when no xStock mirrors this symbol (most stocks). The\nAlpaca side is best-effort - the token price is the point of the call, so\na slow broker feed leaves `market_*` null rather than failing it."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4 - Orders",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "DELETE /orders/{order_id}",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/orders/{{order_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "{{order_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Cancel a working order.\n\nAlpaca's DELETE answers 204 with no body, so we read the order back to\nreport the real outcome. Cancellation is a *request*: an order that is\nstill working goes to `pending_cancel` first and only later to `canceled`.\nAn order that already filled cannot be cancelled at all - Alpaca refuses\nwith 422, which we surface as 409, the honest \"conflicts with current\nstate\" status."
          },
          "response": []
        },
